IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hrq-dates`

-- Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) -- the rules, as the INDIVIDUAL meets them.
--
-- SEAT: an individual affected by an act or decision of a Queensland public entity -- a person injured, held, treated
-- or cared for by the State, a council, the police, a public hospital, a prison (public or privately run), a child
-- safety service or a contractor doing the State's work -- who wants to know what the Act gives them: a complaint to
-- the Queensland Human Rights Commissioner (Part 4, Division 2), and a human rights ground riding on a claim they have
-- apart from the Act (s 59), with no damages of its own (s 59(3)). The public entity, the commissioner, the courts,
-- the Attorney-General and Parliament get no seat.
--
-- In this module: s 8 (compatible with human rights), s 9 and s 10(3) (public entity; functions of a public nature),
-- s 11 (who has human rights), Part 2 (the rights a person in custody or care most relies on, limb by limb: ss 16, 17,
-- 25, 26(2), 29, 30, 31, 33, 37; every right named), s 13 (limits, as a finding), s 45 (effect and life of an override
-- declaration), s 48 (interpretation), s 49 (referral), s 52 (notice to the Attorney-General and the commission: a
-- duty on me as a party, regulative), s 54 (a declaration of incompatibility gives no right), s 58 (conduct of public
-- entities), s 59 (legal proceedings), s 60(3) via s 9(3), ss 63-90 (the complaint, from who may make it to what the
-- commissioner may publish), s 78 (a direction to give information: regulative), s 99 (protection for giving
-- information), s 100 (anonymity direction: regulative), s 102 (address for service), s 108(2) (transitional).
--
-- Judgments the Act leaves to a court or the commissioner (whether a function is of a public nature outside s 10(3),
-- whether treatment was cruel, inhuman or degrading, whether an interference was arbitrary, whether a limit is
-- reasonable and demonstrably justifiable, whether consideration was proper, whether circumstances are exceptional)
-- are inputs, answered conditionally, never decided here.
--
-- Unofficial version. Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026. (c) The State of
-- Queensland, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Human Rights Act 2019: the rules`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 11 -- who has human rights`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 11 "(1) All individuals in Queensland have human rights. (2) Only individuals have human rights." (Note: "A
-- corporation does not have human rights.") (2) closes the list ("only"): a body that is not an individual has none
-- (JUST FALSE kind). (1) speaks of individuals in Queensland and does not say "only": for an individual outside
-- Queensland the Act gives no answer here (NOTHING kind, fork F3).
DECLARE `Who has human rights` IS ONE OF
    `yes: an individual in Queensland has human rights (s 11(1))`
    `no: only individuals have human rights; a corporation or other body has none (s 11(2))`
    `not answered: s 11(1) speaks of individuals in Queensland; for an individual outside Queensland the Act does not say`

GIVEN `an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `in Queensland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Who has human rights`
`s 11 -- has human rights` `an individual` `in Queensland` MEANS
    IF NOT `an individual`
    THEN `no: only individuals have human rights; a corporation or other body has none (s 11(2))`
    ELSE IF `in Queensland`
         THEN `yes: an individual in Queensland has human rights (s 11(1))`
         ELSE `not answered: s 11(1) speaks of individuals in Queensland; for an individual outside Queensland the Act does not say`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 9, 10 -- what a public entity is`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- The kinds of entity s 9 names, in its order. "Government entity within the meaning of the Public Sector Act 2022,
-- section 276", "public service employee", "local government employee", "councillor" and "registered provider" are
-- borrowed: the person picks the kind (fork F4). s 9(5): "entity means an entity in and for Queensland".
DECLARE `Kind of entity` IS ONE OF
    `a government entity, such as a department or a public service office (Public Sector Act 2022, s 276)`
    `a public service employee`
    `the Queensland Police Service, or a police officer`
    `a local government, a councillor or a local government employee`
    `a Minister`
    `an entity established under an Act (for example a hospital and health service, a statutory authority or a public university)`
    `a member of a portfolio committee of Parliament`
    `a staff member or executive officer of a public entity, not otherwise covered`
    `a registered NDIS provider or registered provider of supports`
    `a non-State police officer (for example a Commonwealth officer appointed or authorised under the Police Service Administration Act 1990)`
    `the Legislative Assembly, or a person performing functions in connection with its proceedings`
    `a court or a tribunal`
    `another body or person, not set up under an Act (for example a private company running a prison, a care provider or a contractor)`

-- s 10(3) "Without limiting subsection (1) or (2), the following functions are of a public nature-- (a) the operation
-- of a corrective services facility ... or another place of detention; (b) the provision of any of the following--
-- (i) emergency services; (ii) public health services; (iii) public disability services; (iv) public education ...;
-- (v) public transport; (vi) a housing service by a funded provider or the State under the Housing Act 2003."
DECLARE `Kind of function` IS ONE OF
    `operating a corrective services facility or another place of detention`
    `providing emergency services`
    `providing public health services`
    `providing public disability services`
    `providing public education, including public tertiary or vocational education`
    `providing public transport`
    `providing a housing service as a funded provider or the State under the Housing Act 2003`
    `another function`

-- s 10(3): the listed functions are of a public nature. Any other function is a judgment (s 10(1), (2): factors that
-- "may be considered", not limited): asked as what a court would find.
GIVEN `the function` IS A `Kind of function`, `a court finds it of a public nature` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10 -- of a public nature` `the function` `a court finds it of a public nature` IF
    CONSIDER `the function`
    WHEN `another function` THEN `a court finds it of a public nature`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE `Public entity` IS ONE OF
    `yes: a government entity (s 9(1)(a))`
    `yes: a public service employee (s 9(1)(b))`
    `yes: the Queensland Police Service (s 9(1)(c))`
    `yes: a local government, a councillor or a local government employee (s 9(1)(d))`
    `yes: a Minister (s 9(1)(e))`
    `yes: an entity established under an Act, performing functions of a public nature (s 9(1)(f))`
    `yes: a member of a portfolio committee, the committee acting in an administrative capacity (s 9(1)(g))`
    `yes: an entity performing functions of a public nature for the State or a public entity (s 9(1)(h))`
    `yes: a staff member or executive officer of a public entity (s 9(1)(i))`
    `yes: an entity prescribed by regulation to be a public entity (s 9(1)(j))`
    `yes: a registered provider performing functions of a public nature in the State (s 9(2)(a))`
    `yes: a non-State police officer while appointed, authorised or exercising a power under State law (s 9(2)(b))`
    `yes: an entity that chose to be subject to the obligations, by a declaration in force under s 60 (s 9(3))`
    `no: the Legislative Assembly, or a person performing functions in connection with its proceedings, except when acting in an administrative capacity (s 9(4)(a))`
    `no: a court or tribunal, except when acting in an administrative capacity (s 9(4)(b))`
    `no: an entity prescribed by regulation not to be a public entity (s 9(4)(c))`
    `not shown: none of the kinds in s 9 fits these facts (s 9 does not close its list)`

-- s 9 "(1) Each of the following entities is a public entity-- ... (2) A public entity includes-- ... (3) Also, a public
-- entity includes an entity for which a declaration is in force under section 60. (4) However, a public entity does not
-- include-- (a) the Legislative Assembly or a person performing functions in connection with proceedings in the
-- Assembly, except when acting in an administrative capacity; or (b) a court or tribunal, except when acting in an
-- administrative capacity; or (c) an entity prescribed by regulation not to be a public entity."
-- The exclusions in (4) are flat negatives and come first. s 9 does not close its list (no "means", "includes" twice),
-- so a body in none of its heads is "not shown" (NOTHING kind). A court, tribunal or the Assembly acting in an
-- administrative capacity is not excluded but still needs a head: it is taken under (f) when it performs functions of
-- a public nature (fork F5). The regulations under (1)(j) and (4)(c) are not deposited: asked.
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of entity`
      `the function` IS A `Kind of function`
      `a court finds it of a public nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `performing it for the State or a public entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `acting in an administrative capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `works for a public entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `appointed, authorised or exercising a State power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `prescribed by regulation to be one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `prescribed by regulation not to be one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a s 60 declaration is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Public entity`
`s 9 -- public entity` `the kind` `the function` `a court finds it of a public nature` `performing it for the State or a public entity` `acting in an administrative capacity` `works for a public entity` `appointed, authorised or exercising a State power` `prescribed by regulation to be one` `prescribed by regulation not to be one` `a s 60 declaration is in force` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the kind` EQUALS `the Legislative Assembly, or a person performing functions in connection with its proceedings`) AND (NOT `acting in an administrative capacity`)
        THEN `no: the Legislative Assembly, or a person performing functions in connection with its proceedings, except when acting in an administrative capacity (s 9(4)(a))`
        IF (`the kind` EQUALS `a court or a tribunal`) AND (NOT `acting in an administrative capacity`)
        THEN `no: a court or tribunal, except when acting in an administrative capacity (s 9(4)(b))`
        IF `prescribed by regulation not to be one`
        THEN `no: an entity prescribed by regulation not to be a public entity (s 9(4)(c))`
        IF `the kind` EQUALS `a government entity, such as a department or a public service office (Public Sector Act 2022, s 276)`
        THEN `yes: a government entity (s 9(1)(a))`
        IF `the kind` EQUALS `a public service employee`
        THEN `yes: a public service employee (s 9(1)(b))`
        IF `the kind` EQUALS `the Queensland Police Service, or a police officer`
        THEN `yes: the Queensland Police Service (s 9(1)(c))`
        IF `the kind` EQUALS `a local government, a councillor or a local government employee`
        THEN `yes: a local government, a councillor or a local government employee (s 9(1)(d))`
        IF `the kind` EQUALS `a Minister`
        THEN `yes: a Minister (s 9(1)(e))`
        IF (    (`the kind` EQUALS `an entity established under an Act (for example a hospital and health service, a statutory authority or a public university)`)
             OR (`the kind` EQUALS `a court or a tribunal`)
             OR (`the kind` EQUALS `the Legislative Assembly, or a person performing functions in connection with its proceedings`))
           AND `public nature`
        THEN `yes: an entity established under an Act, performing functions of a public nature (s 9(1)(f))`
        IF (`the kind` EQUALS `a member of a portfolio committee of Parliament`) AND `acting in an administrative capacity`
        THEN `yes: a member of a portfolio committee, the committee acting in an administrative capacity (s 9(1)(g))`
        IF `public nature` AND `performing it for the State or a public entity`
        THEN `yes: an entity performing functions of a public nature for the State or a public entity (s 9(1)(h))`
        IF (`the kind` EQUALS `a staff member or executive officer of a public entity, not otherwise covered`) AND `works for a public entity`
        THEN `yes: a staff member or executive officer of a public entity (s 9(1)(i))`
        IF `prescribed by regulation to be one`
        THEN `yes: an entity prescribed by regulation to be a public entity (s 9(1)(j))`
        IF (`the kind` EQUALS `a registered NDIS provider or registered provider of supports`) AND `public nature`
        THEN `yes: a registered provider performing functions of a public nature in the State (s 9(2)(a))`
        IF (`the kind` EQUALS `a non-State police officer (for example a Commonwealth officer appointed or authorised under the Police Service Administration Act 1990)`) AND `appointed, authorised or exercising a State power`
        THEN `yes: a non-State police officer while appointed, authorised or exercising a power under State law (s 9(2)(b))`
        IF `a s 60 declaration is in force`
        THEN `yes: an entity that chose to be subject to the obligations, by a declaration in force under s 60 (s 9(3))`
        OTHERWISE `not shown: none of the kinds in s 9 fits these facts (s 9 does not close its list)`
    WHERE
        `public nature` MEANS `s 10 -- of a public nature` `the function` `a court finds it of a public nature`

GIVEN `the answer` IS A `Public entity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a public entity` `the answer` IF
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `no: the Legislative Assembly, or a person performing functions in connection with its proceedings, except when acting in an administrative capacity (s 9(4)(a))` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `no: a court or tribunal, except when acting in an administrative capacity (s 9(4)(b))` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `no: an entity prescribed by regulation not to be a public entity (s 9(4)(c))` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `not shown: none of the kinds in s 9 fits these facts (s 9 does not close its list)` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `Part 2 -- the human rights`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 7 "Human rights means the rights stated in part 2, divisions 2 and 3." Every right, by section (ss 15-37). The focus
-- rights are encoded limb by limb below; the others are named so that the s 58 question can be asked of any of them.
DECLARE `Human right` IS ONE OF
    `s 15 recognition and equality before the law`
    `s 16 right to life`
    `s 17 protection from torture and cruel, inhuman or degrading treatment`
    `s 18 freedom from forced work`
    `s 19 freedom of movement`
    `s 20 freedom of thought, conscience, religion and belief`
    `s 21 freedom of expression`
    `s 22 peaceful assembly and freedom of association`
    `s 23 taking part in public life`
    `s 24 property rights`
    `s 25 privacy and reputation`
    `s 26 protection of families and children`
    `s 27 cultural rights generally`
    `s 28 cultural rights of Aboriginal peoples and Torres Strait Islander peoples`
    `s 29 right to liberty and security of person`
    `s 30 humane treatment when deprived of liberty`
    `s 31 fair hearing`
    `s 32 rights in criminal proceedings`
    `s 33 children in the criminal process`
    `s 34 right not to be tried or punished more than once`
    `s 35 retrospective criminal laws`
    `s 36 right to education`
    `s 37 right to health services`

-- The limbs of the focus rights, each a thing the text says a person has a right to, or must not be subjected to.
DECLARE `Right limb` IS ONE OF
    `s 16: the right to life`
    `s 16: arbitrarily deprived of life`
    `s 17(a): subjected to torture`
    `s 17(b): treated or punished in a cruel, inhuman or degrading way`
    `s 17(c): subjected to medical or scientific experimentation or treatment without full, free and informed consent`
    `s 25(a): privacy, family, home or correspondence unlawfully or arbitrarily interfered with`
    `s 25(b): reputation unlawfully attacked`
    `s 26(2): a child not given the protection needed, and in the child's best interests, because of being a child`
    `s 29(1): the right to liberty and security`
    `s 29(2): arbitrary arrest or detention`
    `s 29(3): deprived of liberty other than on grounds, and in accordance with procedures, established by law`
    `s 29(4): not informed at the time of arrest or detention of the reason for it`
    `s 29(4): not promptly informed about proceedings to be brought`
    `s 29(5)(a): not promptly brought before a court on a criminal charge`
    `s 29(5)(b): not brought to trial without unreasonable delay`
    `s 29(5)(c): not released when paragraph (a) or (b) was not complied with`
    `s 29(6): automatically detained in custody while awaiting trial`
    `s 29(7): the court did not decide on the lawfulness of the detention without delay`
    `s 29(7): the court did not order release after finding the detention unlawful`
    `s 29(8): imprisoned only because of an inability to perform a contractual obligation`
    `s 30(1): not treated with humanity and with respect for the inherent dignity of the human person`
    `s 30(2): an unconvicted detainee not segregated from convicted persons, where that was not reasonably necessary`
    `s 30(3): an unconvicted detainee not treated in a way appropriate for a person who has not been convicted`
    `s 31(1): the charge or proceeding not decided by a competent, independent and impartial court or tribunal after a fair and public hearing`
    `s 31(3): the judgment or decision not made publicly available`
    `s 33(1): a detained child not segregated from all detained adults`
    `s 33(2): an accused child not brought to trial as quickly as possible`
    `s 33(3): a convicted child not treated in a way appropriate for the child's age`
    `s 37(1): access to health services refused or limited with discrimination`
    `s 37(2): refused emergency medical treatment immediately necessary to save life or prevent serious impairment`

-- A limb in the list if the facts meet it.
GIVEN `it is met` IS A BOOLEAN, `the limb` IS A `Right limb`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Right limb`
`when` `it is met` `the limb` MEANS
    IF `it is met` THEN LIST `the limb` ELSE EMPTY

-- s 16 "Every person has the right to life and has the right not to be arbitrarily deprived of life." Whether an act or
-- failure (for example a failure to protect a person in custody) limits the first limb is the court's reading, asked.
-- The second limb needs a death (fork F6).
GIVEN `the court holds the right to life was limited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a life was taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `arbitrarily` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Right limb`
`s 16 -- limbs limited` `the court holds the right to life was limited` `a life was taken` `arbitrarily` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`when` `the court holds the right to life was limited` `s 16: the right to life`),
        (`when` (`a life was taken` AND `arbitrarily`) `s 16: arbitrarily deprived of life`))

-- s 17 "A person must not be-- (a) subjected to torture; or (b) treated or punished in a cruel, inhuman or degrading
-- way; or (c) subjected to medical or scientific experimentation or treatment without the person's full, free and
-- informed consent." (a) and (b) are the court's characterisation (asked); (c) turns on facts.
GIVEN `torture` IS A BOOLEAN
      `cruel, inhuman or degrading` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subjected to medical or scientific experimentation or treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `full, free and informed consent given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Right limb`
`s 17 -- limbs limited` `torture` `cruel, inhuman or degrading` `subjected to medical or scientific experimentation or treatment` `full, free and informed consent given` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`when` `torture` `s 17(a): subjected to torture`),
        (`when` `cruel, inhuman or degrading` `s 17(b): treated or punished in a cruel, inhuman or degrading way`),
        (`when` (`subjected to medical or scientific experimentation or treatment` AND (NOT `full, free and informed consent given`)) `s 17(c): subjected to medical or scientific experimentation or treatment without full, free and informed consent`))

-- s 25 "A person has the right-- (a) not to have the person's privacy, family, home or correspondence unlawfully or
-- arbitrarily interfered with; and (b) not to have the person's reputation unlawfully attacked." "Unlawfully" and
-- "arbitrarily" are the court's (asked).
GIVEN `privacy, family, home or correspondence interfered with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interference was unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interference was arbitrary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reputation attacked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the attack was unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Right limb`
`s 25 -- limbs limited` `privacy, family, home or correspondence interfered with` `the interference was unlawful` `the interference was arbitrary` `reputation attacked` `the attack was unlawful` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`when` (`privacy, family, home or correspondence interfered with` AND (`the interference was unlawful` OR `the interference was arbitrary`)) `s 25(a): privacy, family, home or correspondence unlawfully or arbitrarily interfered with`),
        (`when` (`reputation attacked` AND `the attack was unlawful`) `s 25(b): reputation unlawfully attacked`))

-- s 26(2) "Every child has the right, without discrimination, to the protection that is needed by the child, and is in
-- the child's best interests, because of being a child." "Child" is not defined in this Act (borrowed; asked). Whether
-- the protection given fell short is the court's finding (asked).
GIVEN `a child at the time` IS A BOOLEAN, `the protection needed was not given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Right limb`
`s 26(2) -- limbs limited` `a child at the time` `the protection needed was not given` MEANS
    `when` (`a child at the time` AND `the protection needed was not given`) `s 26(2): a child not given the protection needed, and in the child's best interests, because of being a child`

-- s 29 Right to liberty and security of person. (4)-(7) are each limited only where their own conditions hold: (5) for a
-- person arrested or detained on a criminal charge; (6) for a person awaiting trial; (7) where the person applied to a
-- court (fork F7). "Arbitrary", "promptly", "without unreasonable delay", "without delay" are the court's (asked).
GIVEN `the court holds liberty or security was limited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `arrested or detained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the arrest or detention was arbitrary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `deprived of liberty on grounds and by procedures established by law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `told the reason at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `proceedings to be brought` IS A BOOLEAN
      `promptly told about them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on a criminal charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `promptly brought before a court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `brought to trial without unreasonable delay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `released` IS A BOOLEAN
      `automatically detained awaiting trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `applied to a court about the lawfulness of the detention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court decided without delay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court found the detention unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court ordered release` IS A BOOLEAN
      `imprisoned only for inability to perform a contractual obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Right limb`
`s 29 -- limbs limited` `the court holds liberty or security was limited` `arrested or detained` `the arrest or detention was arbitrary` `deprived of liberty on grounds and by procedures established by law` `told the reason at the time` `proceedings to be brought` `promptly told about them` `on a criminal charge` `promptly brought before a court` `brought to trial without unreasonable delay` `released` `automatically detained awaiting trial` `applied to a court about the lawfulness of the detention` `the court decided without delay` `the court found the detention unlawful` `the court ordered release` `imprisoned only for inability to perform a contractual obligation` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`when` `the court holds liberty or security was limited` `s 29(1): the right to liberty and security`),
        (`when` (`arrested or detained` AND `the arrest or detention was arbitrary`) `s 29(2): arbitrary arrest or detention`),
        (`when` (`arrested or detained` AND (NOT `deprived of liberty on grounds and by procedures established by law`)) `s 29(3): deprived of liberty other than on grounds, and in accordance with procedures, established by law`),
        (`when` (`arrested or detained` AND (NOT `told the reason at the time`)) `s 29(4): not informed at the time of arrest or detention of the reason for it`),
        (`when` (`arrested or detained` AND `proceedings to be brought` AND (NOT `promptly told about them`)) `s 29(4): not promptly informed about proceedings to be brought`),
        (`when` (`charged` AND (NOT `promptly brought before a court`)) `s 29(5)(a): not promptly brought before a court on a criminal charge`),
        (`when` (`charged` AND (NOT `brought to trial without unreasonable delay`)) `s 29(5)(b): not brought to trial without unreasonable delay`),
        (`when` (`charged` AND ((NOT `promptly brought before a court`) OR (NOT `brought to trial without unreasonable delay`)) AND (NOT `released`)) `s 29(5)(c): not released when paragraph (a) or (b) was not complied with`),
        (`when` `automatically detained awaiting trial` `s 29(6): automatically detained in custody while awaiting trial`),
        (`when` (`applied` AND (NOT `the court decided without delay`)) `s 29(7): the court did not decide on the lawfulness of the detention without delay`),
        (`when` (`applied` AND `the court found the detention unlawful` AND (NOT `the court ordered release`)) `s 29(7): the court did not order release after finding the detention unlawful`),
        (`when` `imprisoned only for inability to perform a contractual obligation` `s 29(8): imprisoned only because of an inability to perform a contractual obligation`))
    WHERE
        `charged` MEANS `arrested or detained` AND `on a criminal charge`
        `applied` MEANS `arrested or detained` AND `applied to a court about the lawfulness of the detention`

-- s 30 "(1) All persons deprived of liberty must be treated with humanity and with respect for the inherent dignity of
-- the human person. (2) An accused person who is detained or a person detained without charge must be segregated from
-- persons who have been convicted of offences, unless reasonably necessary. (3) An accused person who is detained or a
-- person detained without charge must be treated in a way that is appropriate for a person who has not been
-- convicted." "Deprived of liberty" reaches care and treatment settings as well as custody (asked, fork F8).
GIVEN `deprived of liberty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `treated with humanity and dignity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `unconvicted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `held with convicted persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that was reasonably necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `treated as appropriate for an unconvicted person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Right limb`
`s 30 -- limbs limited` `deprived of liberty` `treated with humanity and dignity` `unconvicted` `held with convicted persons` `that was reasonably necessary` `treated as appropriate for an unconvicted person` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`when` (`deprived of liberty` AND (NOT `treated with humanity and dignity`)) `s 30(1): not treated with humanity and with respect for the inherent dignity of the human person`),
        (`when` (`detained unconvicted` AND `held with convicted persons` AND (NOT `that was reasonably necessary`)) `s 30(2): an unconvicted detainee not segregated from convicted persons, where that was not reasonably necessary`),
        (`when` (`detained unconvicted` AND (NOT `treated as appropriate for an unconvicted person`)) `s 30(3): an unconvicted detainee not treated in a way appropriate for a person who has not been convicted`))
    WHERE
        `detained unconvicted` MEANS `deprived of liberty` AND `unconvicted`

-- s 31 "(1) A person charged with a criminal offence or a party to a civil proceeding has the right to have the charge or
-- proceeding decided by a competent, independent and impartial court or tribunal after a fair and public hearing.
-- (2) However, a court or tribunal may exclude members of media organisations, other persons or the general public
-- from all or part of a hearing in the public interest or the interests of justice. (3) All judgments or decisions made
-- by a court or tribunal in a proceeding must be publicly available." A hearing not public is not a limit where (2)
-- permitted the exclusion (asked).
GIVEN `charged or a party to a civil proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court or tribunal was competent, independent and impartial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hearing was fair` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hearing was public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exclusion was in the public interest or the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judgment or decision is publicly available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Right limb`
`s 31 -- limbs limited` `charged or a party to a civil proceeding` `the court or tribunal was competent, independent and impartial` `the hearing was fair` `the hearing was public` `the exclusion was in the public interest or the interests of justice` `the judgment or decision is publicly available` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`when` (`charged or a party to a civil proceeding` AND
                    (    (NOT `the court or tribunal was competent, independent and impartial`)
                      OR (NOT `the hearing was fair`)
                      OR ((NOT `the hearing was public`) AND (NOT `the exclusion was in the public interest or the interests of justice`))))
            `s 31(1): the charge or proceeding not decided by a competent, independent and impartial court or tribunal after a fair and public hearing`),
        (`when` (`charged or a party to a civil proceeding` AND (NOT `the judgment or decision is publicly available`)) `s 31(3): the judgment or decision not made publicly available`))

-- s 33 "(1) An accused child who is detained, or a child detained without charge, must be segregated from all detained
-- adults. (2) An accused child must be brought to trial as quickly as possible. (3) A child who has been convicted of an
-- offence must be treated in a way that is appropriate for the child's age." No "reasonably necessary" exception in (1),
-- unlike s 30(2) (finding 4).
GIVEN `a child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `accused or detained without charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `convicted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `detained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `held with detained adults` IS A BOOLEAN
      `brought to trial as quickly as possible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `treated as appropriate for my age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Right limb`
`s 33 -- limbs limited` `a child` `accused or detained without charge` `convicted` `detained` `held with detained adults` `brought to trial as quickly as possible` `treated as appropriate for my age` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`when` (`a child` AND `accused or detained without charge` AND `detained` AND `held with detained adults`) `s 33(1): a detained child not segregated from all detained adults`),
        (`when` (`a child` AND `accused or detained without charge` AND (NOT `convicted`) AND (NOT `brought to trial as quickly as possible`)) `s 33(2): an accused child not brought to trial as quickly as possible`),
        (`when` (`a child` AND `convicted` AND (NOT `treated as appropriate for my age`)) `s 33(3): a convicted child not treated in a way appropriate for the child's age`))

-- s 37 "(1) Every person has the right to access health services without discrimination. (2) A person must not be
-- refused emergency medical treatment that is immediately necessary to save the person's life or to prevent serious
-- impairment to the person." "Discrimination" is the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 meaning (schedule 1, borrowed;
-- asked).
GIVEN `access to health services refused or limited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on the basis of an attribute (discrimination)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `refused emergency medical treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `immediately necessary to save my life or prevent serious impairment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Right limb`
`s 37 -- limbs limited` `access to health services refused or limited` `on the basis of an attribute (discrimination)` `refused emergency medical treatment` `immediately necessary to save my life or prevent serious impairment` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`when` (`access to health services refused or limited` AND `on the basis of an attribute (discrimination)`) `s 37(1): access to health services refused or limited with discrimination`),
        (`when` (`refused emergency medical treatment` AND `immediately necessary to save my life or prevent serious impairment`) `s 37(2): refused emergency medical treatment immediately necessary to save life or prevent serious impairment`))

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 8, 13 -- compatible with human rights`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 8 "An act, decision or statutory provision is compatible with human rights if the act, decision or provision--
-- (a) does not limit a human right; or (b) limits a human right only to the extent that is reasonable and demonstrably
-- justifiable in accordance with section 13." s 13(1) "A human right may be subject under law only to reasonable limits
-- that can be demonstrably justified in a free and democratic society ..." The s 13(2) factors are the court's: whether
-- the limit is reasonable and demonstrably justifiable is asked. s 8 is an "if": read as the whole test, so an act that
-- limits a right beyond what s 13 allows is not compatible (fork F9).
DECLARE `Compatibility` IS ONE OF
    `compatible: it limits no human right (s 8(a))`
    `compatible: it limits a human right only to the extent reasonable and demonstrably justifiable under s 13 (s 8(b))`
    `not compatible: it limits a human right beyond what is reasonable and demonstrably justifiable under s 13 (ss 8, 13)`

GIVEN `it limits a human right` IS A BOOLEAN, `the limit is reasonable and demonstrably justifiable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Compatibility`
`s 8 -- compatible with human rights` `it limits a human right` `the limit is reasonable and demonstrably justifiable` MEANS
    IF NOT `it limits a human right`
    THEN `compatible: it limits no human right (s 8(a))`
    ELSE IF `the limit is reasonable and demonstrably justifiable`
         THEN `compatible: it limits a human right only to the extent reasonable and demonstrably justifiable under s 13 (s 8(b))`
         ELSE `not compatible: it limits a human right beyond what is reasonable and demonstrably justifiable under s 13 (ss 8, 13)`

GIVEN `the answer` IS A `Compatibility`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is compatible` `the answer` IF
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `not compatible: it limits a human right beyond what is reasonable and demonstrably justifiable under s 13 (ss 8, 13)` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 58 -- conduct of public entities; s 108(2)(b)`
-- ===================================================================================================================

DECLARE `Unlawful under s 58` IS ONE OF
    `unlawful: the public entity acted or decided in a way not compatible with human rights, and in deciding failed to give proper consideration to a relevant human right (s 58(1)(a) and (b))`
    `unlawful: the public entity acted or decided in a way not compatible with human rights (s 58(1)(a))`
    `unlawful: in making the decision the public entity failed to give proper consideration to a relevant human right (s 58(1)(b))`
    `s 58(1) not met on these facts: the act or decision was compatible with human rights and, for a decision, proper consideration was given`
    `the Act does not apply: an act or decision of a public entity before the commencement (s 108(2)(b))`
    `s 58 does not apply: an act or decision of a private nature (s 58(4))`
    `s 58(1) does not apply: a body established for a religious purpose, acting in accordance with its doctrine and as necessary to avoid offending the religious sensitivities of its people (s 58(3))`
    `s 58(1) does not apply: the public entity could not reasonably have acted or decided differently because of a statutory provision or other law (s 58(2))`
    `s 58 does not reach it: s 58(1) speaks only of a public entity, and the body is not shown to be one (s 9)`

-- s 58 "(1) It is unlawful for a public entity-- (a) to act or make a decision in a way that is not compatible with human
-- rights; or (b) in making a decision, to fail to give proper consideration to a human right relevant to the decision.
-- (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a public entity if the entity could not reasonably have acted differently or made
-- a different decision because of a statutory provision, a law of the Commonwealth or another State or otherwise under
-- law. (3) Also, subsection (1) does not apply to a body established for a religious purpose if the act or decision is
-- done or made in accordance with the doctrine of the religion concerned and is necessary to avoid offending the
-- religious sensitivities of the people of the religion. (4) This section does not apply to an act or decision of a
-- private nature." s 108(2)(b): the Act "does not apply to an act, or decision made, by a public entity before the
-- commencement". Schedule 1: "act includes a failure to act or a proposal to act". The exclusions are flat negatives,
-- tried in the order s 9, s 108(2)(b), s 58(4), (3), (2) (fork F10). Where (1) is not met the answer says so on these
-- facts, never "lawful". s 58(6): an act in contravention is not invalid for that, and is no offence (in the questions'
-- wording).
GIVEN `a public entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `before the commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `of a private nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a religious body acting by its doctrine to avoid offending its people` IS A BOOLEAN
      `could not reasonably have acted differently because of law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `compatibility` IS A `Compatibility`
      `it was a decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a human right was relevant to the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `proper consideration given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Unlawful under s 58`
`s 58 -- unlawful` `a public entity` `before the commencement` `of a private nature` `a religious body acting by its doctrine to avoid offending its people` `could not reasonably have acted differently because of law` `compatibility` `it was a decision` `a human right was relevant to the decision` `proper consideration given` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a public entity`
        THEN `s 58 does not reach it: s 58(1) speaks only of a public entity, and the body is not shown to be one (s 9)`
        IF `before the commencement`
        THEN `the Act does not apply: an act or decision of a public entity before the commencement (s 108(2)(b))`
        IF `of a private nature`
        THEN `s 58 does not apply: an act or decision of a private nature (s 58(4))`
        IF `a religious body acting by its doctrine to avoid offending its people`
        THEN `s 58(1) does not apply: a body established for a religious purpose, acting in accordance with its doctrine and as necessary to avoid offending the religious sensitivities of its people (s 58(3))`
        IF `could not reasonably have acted differently because of law`
        THEN `s 58(1) does not apply: the public entity could not reasonably have acted or decided differently because of a statutory provision or other law (s 58(2))`
        IF `limb a` AND `limb b`
        THEN `unlawful: the public entity acted or decided in a way not compatible with human rights, and in deciding failed to give proper consideration to a relevant human right (s 58(1)(a) and (b))`
        IF `limb a`
        THEN `unlawful: the public entity acted or decided in a way not compatible with human rights (s 58(1)(a))`
        IF `limb b`
        THEN `unlawful: in making the decision the public entity failed to give proper consideration to a relevant human right (s 58(1)(b))`
        OTHERWISE `s 58(1) not met on these facts: the act or decision was compatible with human rights and, for a decision, proper consideration was given`
    WHERE
        `limb a` MEANS NOT (`is compatible` `compatibility`)
        `limb b` MEANS `it was a decision` AND `a human right was relevant to the decision` AND (NOT `proper consideration given`)

GIVEN `the answer` IS A `Unlawful under s 58`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is unlawful under s 58` `the answer` IF
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `unlawful: the public entity acted or decided in a way not compatible with human rights, and in deciding failed to give proper consideration to a relevant human right (s 58(1)(a) and (b))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `unlawful: the public entity acted or decided in a way not compatible with human rights (s 58(1)(a))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `unlawful: in making the decision the public entity failed to give proper consideration to a relevant human right (s 58(1)(b))` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 59 -- legal proceedings: what the Act adds to a claim I already have`
-- ===================================================================================================================

DECLARE `A human rights ground` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I may seek the same relief or remedy on the ground of unlawfulness under s 58, even if I do not succeed on my other ground (s 59(1), (2))`
    `no: I may rely on s 58 unlawfulness only under s 59, which needs a claim to relief or remedy on another ground of unlawfulness (s 59(1), (5))`
    `no ground to add: the act or decision is not shown to be unlawful under s 58`

-- s 59 "(1) Subsection (2) applies if a person may seek any relief or remedy in relation to an act or decision of a
-- public entity on the ground that the act or decision was, other than because of section 58, unlawful. (2) The person
-- may seek the relief or remedy mentioned in subsection (1) on the ground of unlawfulness arising under section 58, even
-- if the person may not be successful in obtaining the relief or remedy on the ground mentioned in subsection (1). ...
-- (5) A person may seek relief or remedy on a ground of unlawfulness arising under section 58 only under this section."
-- (1) is an "if" and (5) says "only": without another ground there is no s 58 ground (JUST FALSE kind). Whether the
-- other claim is one "on the ground that the act or decision was ... unlawful" (for example a claim in negligence) is
-- asked (fork F11).
GIVEN `I have another ground of unlawfulness` IS A BOOLEAN, `unlawful under s 58` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A human rights ground`
`s 59 -- a human rights ground` `I have another ground of unlawfulness` `unlawful under s 58` MEANS
    IF NOT `I have another ground of unlawfulness`
    THEN `no: I may rely on s 58 unlawfulness only under s 59, which needs a claim to relief or remedy on another ground of unlawfulness (s 59(1), (5))`
    ELSE IF `unlawful under s 58`
         THEN `yes: I may seek the same relief or remedy on the ground of unlawfulness under s 58, even if I do not succeed on my other ground (s 59(1), (2))`
         ELSE `no ground to add: the act or decision is not shown to be unlawful under s 58`

DECLARE `Damages` IS ONE OF
    `no damages on the s 58 ground (s 59(3)); the damages my other claim gives are not affected (s 59(6))`
    `no damages on the s 58 ground (s 59(3)), and no other right to damages on these facts`

-- s 59 "(3) However, the person is not entitled to be awarded damages on the ground of unlawfulness arising under section
-- 58. ... (6) Nothing in this section affects a right a person may have to damages apart from the operation of this
-- section." A flat negative: no damages on the s 58 ground, ever.
GIVEN `I have a right to damages apart from this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Damages`
`s 59(3), (6) -- damages` `I have a right to damages apart from this Act` MEANS
    IF `I have a right to damages apart from this Act`
    THEN `no damages on the s 58 ground (s 59(3)); the damages my other claim gives are not affected (s 59(6))`
    ELSE `no damages on the s 58 ground (s 59(3)), and no other right to damages on these facts`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 45, 48, 54, 108(2)(a) -- reading the statutes in my case`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 45(2) "A provision of an Act containing an override declaration expires 5 years after the day on which the provision
-- commences or on an earlier day stated in the Act." Read (fork F12): counting from the day after commencement, the
-- 5 years end at the end of the 5th anniversary of the commencement day, so the provision is in force on that
-- anniversary and expired from the next day; a provision stated to expire on an earlier day is expired on that day.
GIVEN `the day it commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 45(2) -- the last day of an override provision` `the day it commenced` MEANS
    `the anniversary` 5 `years after` `the day it commenced`

-- s 45(1) "If an override declaration is made in relation to an Act or a provision of an Act, this Act does not apply to
-- the Act or provision to the extent of the declaration while the declaration is in force." s 46: a re-enacted
-- declaration runs from its own commencement (the person gives that day).
GIVEN `an override declaration was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it commenced` IS A DATE
      `an earlier expiry day is stated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earlier expiry day` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 45 -- an override declaration is in force` `an override declaration was made` `the day it commenced` `an earlier expiry day is stated` `the earlier expiry day` `the day in question` IF
        `an override declaration was made`
    AND `the day it commenced` `is on or before` `the day in question`
    AND `the day in question` `is on or before` (`s 45(2) -- the last day of an override provision` `the day it commenced`)
    AND (    (NOT `an earlier expiry day is stated`)
         OR  (`the day in question` `is before` `the earlier expiry day`))

-- s 48(1) "All statutory provisions must ..." Schedule 1 "statutory provision means an Act or statutory instrument or a
-- provision of an Act or statutory instrument". "Act" and "statutory instrument" are borrowed (Acts Interpretation Act
-- 1954 and Statutory Instruments Act 1992, not deposited): read as a Queensland Act and an instrument made under one
-- (fork F13).
DECLARE `Kind of law` IS ONE OF
    `a Queensland Act`
    `a Queensland statutory instrument (a regulation, rule or other instrument made under a Queensland Act)`
    `a Commonwealth Act, or an instrument made under one`
    `the common law (judge-made law, such as the law of negligence)`
    `the law of another State, a Territory or another country`

GIVEN `the law` IS A `Kind of law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a statutory provision` `the law` IF
    CONSIDER `the law`
    WHEN `a Queensland Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Queensland statutory instrument (a regulation, rule or other instrument made under a Queensland Act)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Reading compatibly` IS ONE OF
    `yes: so far as possible consistently with its purpose, the provision must be interpreted compatibly with human rights, or else most compatibly (s 48(1), (2)); it stays valid if it cannot be (s 48(4)), and a declaration of incompatibility gives me no right or cause of action (s 54)`
    `no: s 48 does not apply to a provision the subject of an override declaration in force (ss 45(1), 48(5))`
    `no: s 48 applies to statutory provisions, that is Queensland Acts and statutory instruments (schedule 1)`
    `no: the Act does not affect proceedings commenced or concluded before its commencement (s 108(2)(a))`

-- s 48 "(1) All statutory provisions must, to the extent possible that is consistent with their purpose, be interpreted in
-- a way that is compatible with human rights. (2) If a statutory provision can not be interpreted in a way that is
-- compatible with human rights, the provision must, to the extent possible that is consistent with its purpose, be
-- interpreted in a way that is most compatible with human rights. ... (4) This section does not affect the validity
-- of-- (a) an Act or provision of an Act that is not compatible with human rights ... (5) This section does not apply
-- to a statutory provision the subject of an override declaration that is in force." s 54(b): a declaration of
-- incompatibility does not "create in any person any legal right or give rise to any civil cause of action".
-- s 108(2)(a): the Act "does not affect proceedings commenced or concluded before the commencement".
GIVEN `the law` IS A `Kind of law`
      `my proceeding commenced before the commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an override declaration was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it commenced` IS A DATE
      `an earlier expiry day is stated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earlier expiry day` IS A DATE
      `the day of the reading` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Reading compatibly`
`s 48 -- reading compatibly` `the law` `my proceeding commenced before the commencement` `an override declaration was made` `the day it commenced` `an earlier expiry day is stated` `the earlier expiry day` `the day of the reading` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`a statutory provision` `the law`)
        THEN `no: s 48 applies to statutory provisions, that is Queensland Acts and statutory instruments (schedule 1)`
        IF `my proceeding commenced before the commencement`
        THEN `no: the Act does not affect proceedings commenced or concluded before its commencement (s 108(2)(a))`
        IF `s 45 -- an override declaration is in force` `an override declaration was made` `the day it commenced` `an earlier expiry day is stated` `the earlier expiry day` `the day of the reading`
        THEN `no: s 48 does not apply to a provision the subject of an override declaration in force (ss 45(1), 48(5))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: so far as possible consistently with its purpose, the provision must be interpreted compatibly with human rights, or else most compatibly (s 48(1), (2)); it stays valid if it cannot be (s 48(4)), and a declaration of incompatibility gives me no right or cause of action (s 54)`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 49 -- referral of a question to the Supreme Court`
-- ===================================================================================================================

DECLARE `Court` IS ONE OF
    `the Supreme Court (Trial Division)`
    `the District Court`
    `the Land Court`
    `the Land Appeal Court`
    `another court or tribunal (for example the Magistrates Court or QCAT)`

DECLARE `Referral` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the question may be referred to the Supreme Court, and the court must not decide the matter while it is pending or depart from the answer (s 49(2), (3))`
    `yes: the question may be referred to the Court of Appeal, as the referral is by the Trial Division (s 49(2), (4))`
    `no: a referral needs a question of law about the application of the Act, or of interpreting a statutory provision in accordance with it, arising in the proceeding (s 49(1))`
    `no: a referral needs a party's application for it (s 49(2)(a))`
    `no: a referral needs the court or tribunal to consider the question appropriate for the Supreme Court (s 49(2)(b))`

-- s 49 "(1) This section applies if, in a proceeding before a court or tribunal-- (a) a question of law arises that
-- relates to the application of this Act; or (b) a question arises in relation to the interpretation of a statutory
-- provision in accordance with this Act. (2) The question may be referred to the Supreme Court if-- (a) a party to the
-- proceeding has made an application for referral; and (b) the court or tribunal considers the question is appropriate
-- to be decided by the Supreme Court. ... (4) If a question is referred under subsection (2) by the Trial Division of
-- the Supreme Court, the referral is to be made to the Court of Appeal. (5) ... the question may only be referred to the
-- Supreme Court under this section." "If" conditions: no when unmet (JUST FALSE kind).
GIVEN `the court` IS A `Court`
      `a human rights question arises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a party applied for referral` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court considers it appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Referral`
`s 49 -- referral` `the court` `a human rights question arises` `a party applied for referral` `the court considers it appropriate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a human rights question arises`
        THEN `no: a referral needs a question of law about the application of the Act, or of interpreting a statutory provision in accordance with it, arising in the proceeding (s 49(1))`
        IF NOT `a party applied for referral`
        THEN `no: a referral needs a party's application for it (s 49(2)(a))`
        IF NOT `the court considers it appropriate`
        THEN `no: a referral needs the court or tribunal to consider the question appropriate for the Supreme Court (s 49(2)(b))`
        IF `the court` EQUALS `the Supreme Court (Trial Division)`
        THEN `yes: the question may be referred to the Court of Appeal, as the referral is by the Trial Division (s 49(2), (4))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: the question may be referred to the Supreme Court, and the court must not decide the matter while it is pending or depart from the answer (s 49(2), (3))`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 52 -- notice to the Attorney-General and the commission (a duty on me as a party)`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 52 "(1) A party to a proceeding must give notice in the approved form to the Attorney-General and the commission
-- if-- (a) for a proceeding in the Supreme Court, District Court, Land Court or Land Appeal Court--a question of law
-- arises that relates to the application of this Act or a question arises in relation to the interpretation of a
-- statutory provision in accordance with this Act; or (b) for any proceeding--a question is referred to the Supreme
-- Court under section 49. (2) However, the notice need not be given to-- (a) the Attorney-General, if the State is a
-- party to the proceeding; or (b) the commission, if the commission is a party to the proceeding." The approved form
-- (s 104) is not deposited. The Act sets no time for the notice (fork F14).
DECLARE `Notices I must give` IS ONE OF
    `notice in the approved form to both the Attorney-General and the commission (s 52(1))`
    `notice in the approved form to the commission only; none to the Attorney-General, as the State is a party (s 52(1), (2)(a))`
    `notice in the approved form to the Attorney-General only; none to the commission, as it is a party (s 52(1), (2)(b))`
    `no notice: both the State and the commission are parties (s 52(2))`
    `no notice: s 52(1) requires one only for a human rights question in the Supreme, District, Land or Land Appeal Court, or a question referred to the Supreme Court under s 49`

GIVEN `the court` IS A `Court`
      `a human rights question arises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a question was referred under s 49` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 52(1) -- notice is required` `the court` `a human rights question arises` `a question was referred under s 49` IF
        (`a human rights question arises` AND (NOT (`the court` EQUALS `another court or tribunal (for example the Magistrates Court or QCAT)`)))
    OR `a question was referred under s 49`

GIVEN `the court` IS A `Court`
      `a human rights question arises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a question was referred under s 49` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the commission is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Notices I must give`
`s 52 -- notices I must give` `the court` `a human rights question arises` `a question was referred under s 49` `the State is a party` `the commission is a party` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 52(1) -- notice is required` `the court` `a human rights question arises` `a question was referred under s 49`)
        THEN `no notice: s 52(1) requires one only for a human rights question in the Supreme, District, Land or Land Appeal Court, or a question referred to the Supreme Court under s 49`
        IF `the State is a party` AND `the commission is a party`
        THEN `no notice: both the State and the commission are parties (s 52(2))`
        IF `the State is a party`
        THEN `notice in the approved form to the commission only; none to the Attorney-General, as the State is a party (s 52(1), (2)(a))`
        IF `the commission is a party`
        THEN `notice in the approved form to the Attorney-General only; none to the commission, as it is a party (s 52(1), (2)(b))`
        OTHERWISE `notice in the approved form to both the Attorney-General and the commission (s 52(1))`

-- The regulative vocabulary for the three duties encoded as rules (ss 52, 78(5), 100(2)).
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF `I`
DECLARE `Act done` IS ONE OF
    `give notice in the approved form to the Attorney-General`
    `give notice in the approved form to the commission`
    `give the commissioner the information directed`
    `disclose information that identifies the protected person`

-- s 52(1) as a duty on me: I MUST give each notice the section requires (RAND where both are required). No WITHIN: the
-- Act fixes no time, so the duty waits until done (fork F14); the Act says nothing of what follows a failure, so no LEST.
GIVEN `the notices` IS A `Notices I must give`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act done`
`s 52(1) -- my duty to notify` `the notices` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the notices`
    WHEN `notice in the approved form to both the Attorney-General and the commission (s 52(1))` THEN
        (PARTY `I` MUST `give notice in the approved form to the Attorney-General`)
        RAND
        (PARTY `I` MUST `give notice in the approved form to the commission`)
    WHEN `notice in the approved form to the commission only; none to the Attorney-General, as the State is a party (s 52(1), (2)(a))` THEN
        PARTY `I` MUST `give notice in the approved form to the commission`
    WHEN `notice in the approved form to the Attorney-General only; none to the commission, as it is a party (s 52(1), (2)(b))` THEN
        PARTY `I` MUST `give notice in the approved form to the Attorney-General`
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED

-- Runs the duty over what I have done. A CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE matches FULFILLED only; a duty still waiting is a
-- residual, so not FULFILLED. Takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Party` `Act done`
      `I gave the Attorney-General notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I gave the commission notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice duty is met under` `the rule` `I gave the Attorney-General notice` `I gave the commission notice` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (IF `I gave the Attorney-General notice` AND `I gave the commission notice`
                                     THEN LIST (EVENT `I` `give notice in the approved form to the Attorney-General` 1), (EVENT `I` `give notice in the approved form to the commission` 1)
                                     ELSE IF `I gave the Attorney-General notice`
                                          THEN LIST (EVENT `I` `give notice in the approved form to the Attorney-General` 1)
                                          ELSE IF `I gave the commission notice`
                                               THEN LIST (EVENT `I` `give notice in the approved form to the commission` 1)
                                               ELSE LIST (WAITUNTIL 1))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Notices given` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I have given every notice s 52 requires`
    `yes: s 52 requires no notice from me`
    `no: I have still to give a notice s 52 requires`

GIVEN `the court` IS A `Court`
      `a human rights question arises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a question was referred under s 49` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the commission is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I gave the Attorney-General notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I gave the commission notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Notices given`
`s 52 -- have I given the notices` `the court` `a human rights question arises` `a question was referred under s 49` `the State is a party` `the commission is a party` `I gave the Attorney-General notice` `I gave the commission notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the notices`
    WHEN `no notice: both the State and the commission are parties (s 52(2))` THEN `yes: s 52 requires no notice from me`
    WHEN `no notice: s 52(1) requires one only for a human rights question in the Supreme, District, Land or Land Appeal Court, or a question referred to the Supreme Court under s 49` THEN `yes: s 52 requires no notice from me`
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the notice duty is met under` (`s 52(1) -- my duty to notify` `the notices`) `I gave the Attorney-General notice` `I gave the commission notice`
        THEN `yes: I have given every notice s 52 requires`
        ELSE `no: I have still to give a notice s 52 requires`
    WHERE
        `the notices` MEANS `s 52 -- notices I must give` `the court` `a human rights question arises` `a question was referred under s 49` `the State is a party` `the commission is a party`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 63, 64 -- who may complain to the commissioner`
-- ===================================================================================================================

DECLARE `Who I am` IS ONE OF
    `the individual the public entity's alleged contravention was about`
    `an agent of that individual`
    `a person the commissioner has authorised in writing to complain for the individual`
    `someone else (for example a relative or an organisation that is not the individual's agent)`

DECLARE `May I complain` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the individual the subject of the alleged contravention (s 64(1)(a))`
    `yes: an agent of the individual (s 64(1)(b))`
    `yes: a person authorised in writing by the commissioner, who must be satisfied the individual can not make the complaint (s 64(1)(c), (2))`
    `not yet: the commissioner may authorise you in writing only if satisfied the individual can not make the complaint (s 64(2))`
    `no: a human rights complaint is about an alleged contravention of s 58(1) by a public entity (s 63)`
    `not shown: s 64 does not list you; an agent of the individual, or a person the commissioner authorises, may complain`

-- s 63 "A human rights complaint is a complaint about an alleged contravention of section 58(1) by a public entity in
-- relation to an act or decision of the public entity." A "means"-like definition: a complaint about a body that is not
-- a public entity is not one (JUST FALSE kind). s 64 "(1) The following persons may make a human rights complaint to
-- the commissioner-- (a) an individual the subject of a public entity's alleged contravention of section 58(1); (b) an
-- agent of the individual; (c) a person authorised in writing by the commissioner to make a complaint for the
-- individual. (2) ... the commissioner may authorise a person ... if satisfied the individual can not make the
-- complaint. (3) Two or more persons may jointly make a human rights complaint." The list is not closed by "only": for
-- anyone else, NOTHING kind.
GIVEN `who I am` IS A `Who I am`
      `about a public entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the commissioner is satisfied the individual can not complain` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `May I complain`
`ss 63, 64 -- may I complain` `who I am` `about a public entity` `the commissioner is satisfied the individual can not complain` MEANS
    IF NOT `about a public entity`
    THEN `no: a human rights complaint is about an alleged contravention of s 58(1) by a public entity (s 63)`
    ELSE CONSIDER `who I am`
         WHEN `the individual the public entity's alleged contravention was about` THEN `yes: the individual the subject of the alleged contravention (s 64(1)(a))`
         WHEN `an agent of that individual` THEN `yes: an agent of the individual (s 64(1)(b))`
         WHEN `a person the commissioner has authorised in writing to complain for the individual` THEN
             IF `the commissioner is satisfied the individual can not complain`
             THEN `yes: a person authorised in writing by the commissioner, who must be satisfied the individual can not make the complaint (s 64(1)(c), (2))`
             ELSE `not yet: the commissioner may authorise you in writing only if satisfied the individual can not make the complaint (s 64(2))`
         OTHERWISE `not shown: s 64 does not list you; an agent of the individual, or a person the commissioner authorises, may complain`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 65 -- complaining to the public entity first, and waiting 45 business days`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 65(1)(b) "at least 45 business days have elapsed since the complaint mentioned in paragraph (a) was made". Read
-- (fork F15): business days are counted from the day after the complaint to the public entity; 45 have elapsed at the
-- end of the 45th, so the earliest day to complain to the commissioner is the next calendar day.
GIVEN `the day I complained to the public entity` IS A DATE, `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 65(1)(b) -- the earliest day` `the day I complained to the public entity` `the public holidays` MEANS
    1 `days after` (`the business day after` 45 `the day I complained to the public entity` `the public holidays`)

DECLARE `Can I complain now` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you complained to the public entity, at least 45 business days have passed, and you have had no response or one you consider inadequate (s 65(1))`
    `yes, early: the commissioner may accept it before the 45 business days have passed, as the commissioner considers it appropriate because of exceptional circumstances (s 65(2))`
    `not yet: 45 business days have not passed since you complained to the public entity (s 65(1)(b)); see the earliest day`
    `no: you must first complain to the public entity about the alleged contravention (s 65(1)(a))`
    `no: you have had a response from the public entity that you do not consider inadequate (s 65(1)(c))`

-- s 65 "(1) A person may make a human rights complaint to the commissioner only if-- (a) the commissioner is satisfied
-- the person has made a complaint to the public entity about the alleged contravention ...; and (b) at least 45
-- business days have elapsed since the complaint mentioned in paragraph (a) was made; and (c) the person has not
-- received a response to the complaint or has received a response the person considers to be an inadequate response.
-- (2) However, the commissioner may accept a complaint made before the period mentioned in subsection (1)(b) has
-- elapsed if the commissioner considers it appropriate because of exceptional circumstances." "Only if": each unmet
-- condition is a no (JUST FALSE kind). (2) lifts only (b). Whether the commissioner is satisfied (a) and considers
-- circumstances exceptional (2) are asked.
GIVEN `I complained to the public entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I complained to the public entity` IS A DATE
      `the day I complain to the commissioner` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `I had a response` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I consider the response inadequate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the commissioner considers there are exceptional circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Can I complain now`
`s 65 -- can I complain now` `I complained to the public entity` `the day I complained to the public entity` `the day I complain to the commissioner` `the public holidays` `I had a response` `I consider the response inadequate` `the commissioner considers there are exceptional circumstances` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `I complained to the public entity`
        THEN `no: you must first complain to the public entity about the alleged contravention (s 65(1)(a))`
        IF `I had a response` AND (NOT `I consider the response inadequate`)
        THEN `no: you have had a response from the public entity that you do not consider inadequate (s 65(1)(c))`
        IF (`s 65(1)(b) -- the earliest day` `the day I complained to the public entity` `the public holidays`) `is on or before` `the day I complain to the commissioner`
        THEN `yes: you complained to the public entity, at least 45 business days have passed, and you have had no response or one you consider inadequate (s 65(1))`
        IF `the commissioner considers there are exceptional circumstances`
        THEN `yes, early: the commissioner may accept it before the 45 business days have passed, as the commissioner considers it appropriate because of exceptional circumstances (s 65(2))`
        OTHERWISE `not yet: 45 business days have not passed since you complained to the public entity (s 65(1)(b)); see the earliest day`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 70(1)(d) -- the 1-year time limit`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 70(1)(d) "the complaint was not made or referred to the commissioner within 1 year after the alleged contravention
-- to which the complaint relates happened." Read (fork F2): the year runs from the day after the contravention and ends
-- at the end of its anniversary (for 29 February, 28 February).
GIVEN `the day of the contravention` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 70(1)(d) -- the last day` `the day of the contravention` MEANS
    `the anniversary` 1 `years after` `the day of the contravention`

DECLARE `Time limit` IS ONE OF
    `in time: made within 1 year after the alleged contravention, so s 70(1)(d) gives no ground to refuse`
    `late: the commissioner may refuse to deal with it under s 70(1)(d) (a discretion, not a bar); if refused, it lapses and you can not complain again about it (s 72)`

-- "may refuse": the commissioner's discretion is not decided. Outside the period the answer is the discretion, worded as
-- such.
GIVEN `the day of the contravention` IS A DATE, `the day I complain to the commissioner` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`s 70(1)(d) -- in time` `the day of the contravention` `the day I complain to the commissioner` MEANS
    IF `the day I complain to the commissioner` `is on or before` (`s 70(1)(d) -- the last day` `the day of the contravention`)
    THEN `in time: made within 1 year after the alleged contravention, so s 70(1)(d) gives no ground to refuse`
    ELSE `late: the commissioner may refuse to deal with it under s 70(1)(d) (a discretion, not a bar); if refused, it lapses and you can not complain again about it (s 72)`

-- The two periods together: the earliest day under s 65(1)(b) against the last day under s 70(1)(d).
DECLARE `Both periods` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you can wait the 45 business days and still complain within the year; the window is from the earliest day to the last day`
    `no: the 45 business days end after the 1-year limit; you would need the commissioner to accept the complaint early for exceptional circumstances (s 65(2)) or not to refuse it as late (s 70(1)(d))`

GIVEN `the day of the contravention` IS A DATE
      `the day I complained to the public entity` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A `Both periods`
`ss 65, 70 -- can I meet both periods` `the day of the contravention` `the day I complained to the public entity` `the public holidays` MEANS
    IF (`s 65(1)(b) -- the earliest day` `the day I complained to the public entity` `the public holidays`) `is on or before` (`s 70(1)(d) -- the last day` `the day of the contravention`)
    THEN `yes: you can wait the 45 business days and still complain within the year; the window is from the earliest day to the last day`
    ELSE `no: the 45 business days end after the 1-year limit; you would need the commissioner to accept the complaint early for exceptional circumstances (s 65(2)) or not to refuse it as late (s 70(1)(d))`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 67, 102 -- the form of the complaint`
-- ===================================================================================================================

DECLARE `Kind of address` IS ONE OF
    `a residential address`
    `a business address`
    `a post office box address`
    `an email address`
    `none, or another kind`

DECLARE `Form of complaint` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the complaint is in writing, states your name and an address for service, and has enough detail of the alleged contravention (ss 67(1), 102)`
    `no: it must be written; the commissioner must give you reasonable help to put it in writing if satisfied you need it (s 67(1)(a), (2))`
    `no: it must state your name and an address for service: a residential or business address, a post office box or an email address (ss 67(1)(b), 102)`
    `no: it must include enough details to indicate the alleged contravention (s 67(1)(c))`

-- s 67 "(1) A human rights complaint made or referred to the commissioner must-- (a) be written; and (b) state the
-- complainant's name and address for service; and (c) include enough details to indicate the alleged contravention to
-- which the complaint relates. (2) If the commissioner is satisfied the complainant needs help to put the complaint in
-- writing, the commissioner must give reasonable help ..." s 102 "The address for service ... must be a residential or
-- business address, a post office box address, or an email address." A bare "must" not met: taken as "no" with the
-- requirement (Meng's case-by-case rule; fork F16).
GIVEN `it is written` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states my name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the address` IS A `Kind of address`
      `it has enough details of the alleged contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Form of complaint`
`ss 67, 102 -- form of complaint` `it is written` `it states my name` `the address` `it has enough details of the alleged contravention` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it is written`
        THEN `no: it must be written; the commissioner must give you reasonable help to put it in writing if satisfied you need it (s 67(1)(a), (2))`
        IF (NOT `it states my name`) OR (`the address` EQUALS `none, or another kind`)
        THEN `no: it must state your name and an address for service: a residential or business address, a post office box or an email address (ss 67(1)(b), 102)`
        IF NOT `it has enough details of the alleged contravention`
        THEN `no: it must include enough details to indicate the alleged contravention (s 67(1)(c))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: the complaint is in writing, states your name and an address for service, and has enough detail of the alleged contravention (ss 67(1), 102)`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 69-72 -- refusal, deferral and lapse`
-- ===================================================================================================================

DECLARE `What the commissioner did` IS ONE OF
    `refused it as frivolous, trivial, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance (s 69)`
    `refused it as there is a more appropriate course under another law (s 70(1)(a))`
    `refused it as already appropriately dealt with by another entity (s 70(1)(b))`
    `refused it as the s 65 requirements were not met (s 70(1)(c))`
    `refused it as not made within 1 year after the contravention (s 70(1)(d))`
    `refused to continue as I did not comply with a reasonable request (s 70(2)(a))`
    `refused to continue as I did not cooperate without reasonable excuse (s 70(2)(b))`
    `refused to continue as I could not be contacted (s 70(2)(c))`
    `deferred dealing with it (s 70(3))`

DECLARE `After refusal` IS ONE OF
    `the complaint lapses, and you can not make a further complaint about the same alleged contravention (s 72(1)); you must be given notice of the refusal and the reasons (s 71(1))`
    `the complaint lapses, but you may complain again about the same contravention once the s 65 requirements are met, as the refusal was under s 70(1)(c) (s 72(1)(a), (2)); you must be given notice of the refusal and the reasons (s 71(1))`
    `the complaint does not lapse: s 72 speaks only of refusal; a deferral keeps it alive, and you must be given notice of the deferral and the reasons (s 71(1))`

-- s 72 "(1) If the commissioner refuses to deal, or to continue to deal, with a human rights complaint-- (a) the
-- complaint lapses; and (b) the complainant can not make a further complaint relating to the alleged contravention the
-- subject of the complaint. (2) Subsection (1)(b) does not apply to a human rights complaint the commissioner refuses to
-- deal with under section 70(1)(c)." s 71(1): notice of the refusal or deferral, and the reasons. The s 70(1)(c)
-- exception reaches only a refusal "to deal" (not "to continue to deal"); s 70(1)(c) is in (1), which covers both.
-- Taken as covering both (fork F17).
GIVEN `what the commissioner did` IS A `What the commissioner did`
GIVETH A `After refusal`
`ss 71, 72 -- after refusal` `what the commissioner did` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what the commissioner did`
    WHEN `deferred dealing with it (s 70(3))` THEN `the complaint does not lapse: s 72 speaks only of refusal; a deferral keeps it alive, and you must be given notice of the deferral and the reasons (s 71(1))`
    WHEN `refused it as the s 65 requirements were not met (s 70(1)(c))` THEN `the complaint lapses, but you may complain again about the same contravention once the s 65 requirements are met, as the refusal was under s 70(1)(c) (s 72(1)(a), (2)); you must be given notice of the refusal and the reasons (s 71(1))`
    OTHERWISE `the complaint lapses, and you can not make a further complaint about the same alleged contravention (s 72(1)); you must be given notice of the refusal and the reasons (s 71(1))`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 66, 73, 75 -- passing the complaint to another body (only with my consent)`
-- ===================================================================================================================

DECLARE `Where to` IS ONE OF
    `the ombudsman, the health ombudsman, the Crime and Corruption Commission, the information commissioner or the NDIS commissioner (s 73)`
    `dealt with by the commission as an Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 complaint (s 75)`
    `from the ombudsman, health ombudsman, Crime and Corruption Commission or information commissioner to the human rights commissioner (s 66)`

DECLARE `Passing on` IS ONE OF
    `yes: with your consent, and as the commissioner considers it more appropriately dealt with there (s 73(6)); the commissioner must tell you it has been referred (s 73(7)(b))`
    `yes: with your consent, the commissioner may deal with it under the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991, as made on the day of your human rights complaint (s 75(2), (3))`
    `yes: with your consent, the referral entity may refer it to the human rights commissioner (s 66(2)(b))`
    `no: it may be passed on only with your consent (ss 66(2)(b), 73(6)(a), 75(2))`
    `no: the commissioner may refer it only if the commissioner considers it would be more appropriately dealt with there (s 73(6)(b))`

-- s 73(6) "However, the commissioner may only refer a human rights complaint under this section-- (a) with the
-- complainant's consent; and (b) if the commissioner considers the complaint would be more appropriately dealt with by
-- the entity". s 75(1), (2): where the commissioner considers it more appropriately dealt with under the Anti-
-- Discrimination Act 1991, "with the consent of the complainant". s 66(2)(b): "with the consent of the person who could
-- make the human rights complaint". "Only" and "with the consent" are closed: without consent, no.
GIVEN `where to` IS A `Where to`
      `I consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the commissioner considers it more appropriate there` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Passing on`
`ss 66, 73, 75 -- passing on` `where to` `I consent` `the commissioner considers it more appropriate there` MEANS
    IF NOT `I consent`
    THEN `no: it may be passed on only with your consent (ss 66(2)(b), 73(6)(a), 75(2))`
    ELSE CONSIDER `where to`
         WHEN `from the ombudsman, health ombudsman, Crime and Corruption Commission or information commissioner to the human rights commissioner (s 66)` THEN `yes: with your consent, the referral entity may refer it to the human rights commissioner (s 66(2)(b))`
         OTHERWISE
             IF NOT `the commissioner considers it more appropriate there`
             THEN `no: the commissioner may refer it only if the commissioner considers it would be more appropriately dealt with there (s 73(6)(b))`
             ELSE CONSIDER `where to`
                  WHEN `dealt with by the commission as an Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 complaint (s 75)` THEN `yes: with your consent, the commissioner may deal with it under the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991, as made on the day of your human rights complaint (s 75(2), (3))`
                  OTHERWISE `yes: with your consent, and as the commissioner considers it more appropriately dealt with there (s 73(6)); the commissioner must tell you it has been referred (s 73(7)(b))`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 71, 73(7), 76, 88, 89 -- what the commissioner must give me`
-- ===================================================================================================================

DECLARE `Stage` IS ONE OF
    `the commissioner refused to deal, or to continue to deal, with my complaint`
    `the commissioner deferred dealing with my complaint`
    `the commissioner referred my complaint to another entity`
    `the commissioner accepted my complaint for resolution`
    `the commission finished dealing with my complaint and it was not resolved`
    `my complaint was resolved`

DECLARE `What I must be given` IS ONE OF
    `notice of the refusal and the reasons for it (s 71(1))`
    `notice of the deferral and the reasons for it (s 71(1))`
    `a notice stating the complaint has been referred to the entity (s 73(7)(b))`
    `notice of the acceptance, stating the commission's role in trying to resolve it and the commissioner's powers (s 76(1), (2))`
    `a copy of the commissioner's report on the unresolved complaint, prepared as soon as practicable, with its substance and the actions taken (s 88(2), (3), (5))`
    `as soon as practicable, a notice stating the outcome and that the commission has finished dealing with the complaint (s 89(2))`

GIVEN `the stage` IS A `Stage`
GIVETH A `What I must be given`
`what the commissioner must give me` `the stage` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the stage`
    WHEN `the commissioner refused to deal, or to continue to deal, with my complaint` THEN `notice of the refusal and the reasons for it (s 71(1))`
    WHEN `the commissioner deferred dealing with my complaint` THEN `notice of the deferral and the reasons for it (s 71(1))`
    WHEN `the commissioner referred my complaint to another entity` THEN `a notice stating the complaint has been referred to the entity (s 73(7)(b))`
    WHEN `the commissioner accepted my complaint for resolution` THEN `notice of the acceptance, stating the commission's role in trying to resolve it and the commissioner's powers (s 76(1), (2))`
    WHEN `the commission finished dealing with my complaint and it was not resolved` THEN `a copy of the commissioner's report on the unresolved complaint, prepared as soon as practicable, with its substance and the actions taken (s 88(2), (3), (5))`
    WHEN `my complaint was resolved` THEN `as soon as practicable, a notice stating the outcome and that the commission has finished dealing with the complaint (s 89(2))`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 78 -- a direction to give the commissioner information (a duty on me as complainant)`
-- ===================================================================================================================

DECLARE `Information duty` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you must comply with the direction within the period stated in the notice; the commissioner may file it with a court and it is then enforceable as a court order (s 78(5), (7), (8))`
    `no: you need not comply, as you have a reasonable excuse, such as legal professional privilege (s 78(5), (6))`
    `no duty: a request is not a direction, but if it is a reasonable request and you do not comply the commissioner may refuse to continue with your complaint (s 70(2)(a))`
    `no: a notice under s 78 must state the purpose of the request; this one does not (s 78(3))`

-- s 78 "(2) The commissioner may, by notice given to a relevant entity for the complaint, ask or direct the entity to give
-- the commissioner information about the complaint within the reasonable period stated in the notice. (3) The notice
-- must state the purpose for making the request. ... (5) The entity must comply with a direction unless the entity has
-- a reasonable excuse. (6) It is a reasonable excuse ... because ... complying with the direction would require the
-- entity to disclose information that is the subject of legal professional privilege. (7) The commissioner may enforce
-- a direction by filing a copy of it with a court ... (8) The direction is then enforceable as if it were an order of
-- the court." The complainant is a "relevant entity" (s 78(9)). A notice without its purpose: taken as giving no duty
-- (a bare "must" not met; fork F18).
GIVEN `it is a direction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states its purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Information duty`
`s 78 -- must I give the information` `it is a direction` `the notice states its purpose` `I have a reasonable excuse` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the notice states its purpose`
        THEN `no: a notice under s 78 must state the purpose of the request; this one does not (s 78(3))`
        IF NOT `it is a direction`
        THEN `no duty: a request is not a direction, but if it is a reasonable request and you do not comply the commissioner may refuse to continue with your complaint (s 70(2)(a))`
        IF `I have a reasonable excuse`
        THEN `no: you need not comply, as you have a reasonable excuse, such as legal professional privilege (s 78(5), (6))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: you must comply with the direction within the period stated in the notice; the commissioner may file it with a court and it is then enforceable as a court order (s 78(5), (7), (8))`

-- The regulative rule. s 78(2), (5): I MUST give the information WITHIN the days from the notice to the end of the
-- period stated. LEST: the Act's consequences of not complying (enforceable as a court order once filed, s 78(7), (8);
-- and the commissioner may refuse to continue, s 70(2)(a)).
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act done`
`s 78(5) -- my duty to give the information` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `I`
    MUST `give the commissioner the information directed`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `I` BECAUSE "a direction under s 78 not complied with within the period stated: enforceable as a court order once filed (s 78(7), (8)); the commissioner may refuse to continue with the complaint (s 70(2)(a))"

DECLARE `Complied in time` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you gave the information within the period stated in the direction`
    `no: you have not given the information within the period stated in the direction`
    `no duty to comply on these facts (see the s 78 question)`

-- Runs the s 78 duty over the days: the notice day is day 0; the information was given on the day I gave it (if I did);
-- the trace waits to the day after the last day of the period.
GIVEN `the duty` IS A `Information duty`
      `the day of the notice` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE
      `I gave it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I gave it` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Complied in time`
`s 78 -- complied in time` `the duty` `the day of the notice` `the last day of the period` `I gave it` `the day I gave it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the duty`
    WHEN `yes: you must comply with the direction within the period stated in the notice; the commissioner may file it with a court and it is then enforceable as a court order (s 78(5), (7), (8))` THEN
        CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 78(5) -- my duty to give the information` `the days allowed`) 0
                           (IF `I gave it`
                            THEN LIST (EVENT `I` `give the commissioner the information directed` (`the number of days from` `the day of the notice` `until` `the day I gave it`)), (WAITUNTIL (`the days allowed` PLUS 1))
                            ELSE LIST (WAITUNTIL (`the days allowed` PLUS 1)))
        WHEN FULFILLED THEN `yes: you gave the information within the period stated in the direction`
        OTHERWISE `no: you have not given the information within the period stated in the direction`
    OTHERWISE `no duty to comply on these facts (see the s 78 question)`
    WHERE
        `the days allowed` MEANS `the number of days from` `the day of the notice` `until` `the last day of the period`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 82-84 -- the conciliation conference (only if the commissioner holds one)`
-- ===================================================================================================================

DECLARE `Attend in person` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you must attend in person; with the commissioner's consent you may bring a support person, and you may be helped by an interpreter or another person needed to make it intelligible (ss 82(1), (2), 84)`
    `no: a child need not attend in person (s 82(1)(a))`
    `no: a person with impaired capacity need not attend in person (s 82(1)(a))`
    `no: the commissioner has consented to another person attending for you (s 82(1)(b))`

-- s 82(1) "The complainant ... must attend the conciliation conference in person unless-- (a) the complainant is a child
-- or a person with impaired capacity; or (b) the commissioner consents to another person attending the conciliation
-- conference for the complainant." "Child" (not defined here) and "impaired capacity" (Guardianship and Administration
-- Act 2000, schedule 4; not deposited) are asked. "Unless" once met: taken as no duty (fork F19).
GIVEN `I am a child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have impaired capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the commissioner consented to another person attending for me` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Attend in person`
`s 82 -- must I attend in person` `I am a child` `I have impaired capacity` `the commissioner consented to another person attending for me` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `I am a child` THEN `no: a child need not attend in person (s 82(1)(a))`
        IF `I have impaired capacity` THEN `no: a person with impaired capacity need not attend in person (s 82(1)(a))`
        IF `the commissioner consented to another person attending for me` THEN `no: the commissioner has consented to another person attending for you (s 82(1)(b))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: you must attend in person; with the commissioner's consent you may bring a support person, and you may be helped by an interpreter or another person needed to make it intelligible (ss 82(1), (2), 84)`

DECLARE `Representation` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the commissioner has consented, on any reasonable conditions, which can be withdrawn if they are not complied with (s 83(1), (3))`
    `no: you may be represented at a conciliation conference only with the commissioner's consent (s 83(1))`

-- s 83(1) "A person may be represented by another person (a representative) at a conciliation conference only with the
-- commissioner's consent." "Only": without consent, no (JUST FALSE kind). The (2) grounds for consent are the
-- commissioner's.
GIVEN `the commissioner consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Representation`
`s 83 -- may I be represented` `the commissioner consented` MEANS
    IF `the commissioner consented`
    THEN `yes: the commissioner has consented, on any reasonable conditions, which can be withdrawn if they are not complied with (s 83(1), (3))`
    ELSE `no: you may be represented at a conciliation conference only with the commissioner's consent (s 83(1))`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 86, 88(6) -- can the conference or the report be used in court`
-- ===================================================================================================================

DECLARE `What I want to use` IS ONE OF
    `something said or done in the conciliation conference`
    `the commissioner's report on my unresolved complaint`

DECLARE `Kind of proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `a proceeding about a contravention of the Human Rights Act`
    `another civil, criminal or administrative proceeding (for example my claim in negligence)`

DECLARE `Admissible` IS ONE OF
    `yes: both you and the respondent agree (ss 86, 88(6))`
    `no: nothing said or done in a conciliation conference is admissible in any criminal, civil or administrative proceeding unless you and the respondent agree (s 86)`
    `no: the report is not admissible in a proceeding about a contravention of the Act unless you and the respondent agree (s 88(6))`
    `not answered: s 88(6) speaks only of a proceeding about a contravention of this Act; for another proceeding the Act does not say`

-- s 86 "Nothing said or done in the course of a conciliation conference ... is admissible in any criminal, civil or
-- administrative proceeding, unless the complainant and respondent for the complaint agree." s 88(6) "The report is not
-- admissible in a proceeding in relation to a contravention of this Act, unless the complainant and respondent agree."
-- Flat negatives with "unless". The report in another proceeding: the text is silent (NOTHING kind; finding 5).
GIVEN `what` IS A `What I want to use`
      `the proceeding` IS A `Kind of proceeding`
      `both agree` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Admissible`
`ss 86, 88(6) -- admissible` `what` `the proceeding` `both agree` MEANS
    IF `both agree`
    THEN `yes: both you and the respondent agree (ss 86, 88(6))`
    ELSE CONSIDER `what`
         WHEN `something said or done in the conciliation conference` THEN `no: nothing said or done in a conciliation conference is admissible in any criminal, civil or administrative proceeding unless you and the respondent agree (s 86)`
         OTHERWISE
             IF `the proceeding` EQUALS `a proceeding about a contravention of the Human Rights Act`
             THEN `no: the report is not admissible in a proceeding about a contravention of the Act unless you and the respondent agree (s 88(6))`
             ELSE `not answered: s 88(6) speaks only of a proceeding about a contravention of this Act; for another proceeding the Act does not say`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 90 -- publication of information about my complaint`
-- ===================================================================================================================

DECLARE `Publication` IS ONE OF
    `the commissioner may publish information about the complaint, including your personal information, as you have published it or given it for publication before (s 90(1), (2)(c))`
    `the commissioner may publish information about the complaint, but not your personal information (s 90(1), (2)(c))`
    `not answered: s 90(1) gives the power to publish for a complaint the commission has finished dealing with; for one still open the Act does not say`

-- s 90 "(1) The commissioner may publish information about a human rights complaint that the commission has finished
-- dealing with. (2) The publication-- ... (c) must not include personal information about an individual unless the
-- information has previously been published, or given for the purpose of publication, by the individual." "Personal
-- information" is the Information Privacy Act 2009 term (asked by its plain sense). (1) limits the grant to finished
-- complaints without "only": before then, not answered (NOTHING kind, fork F20).
GIVEN `the commission has finished dealing with it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I published it or gave it for publication before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Publication`
`s 90 -- publication` `the commission has finished dealing with it` `I published it or gave it for publication before` MEANS
    IF NOT `the commission has finished dealing with it`
    THEN `not answered: s 90(1) gives the power to publish for a complaint the commission has finished dealing with; for one still open the Act does not say`
    ELSE IF `I published it or gave it for publication before`
         THEN `the commissioner may publish information about the complaint, including your personal information, as you have published it or given it for publication before (s 90(1), (2)(c))`
         ELSE `the commissioner may publish information about the complaint, but not your personal information (s 90(1), (2)(c))`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 99 -- protection for giving information`
-- ===================================================================================================================

DECLARE `Protected` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you are not liable civilly, criminally or under an administrative process for giving it, and are not taken to have breached professional ethics or standards (s 99(2), (3))`
    `no: s 99 gives no protection on these facts; it applies to information given honestly under the Act to the commissioner or another entity about a human rights complaint (s 99(1))`

-- s 99 "(1) This section applies if a person, acting honestly, gives information under this Act to the commissioner or
-- another entity in relation to a human rights complaint. (2) The person is not liable, civilly, criminally or under an
-- administrative process, for giving the information. (3) Also, merely because the person gives the information, the
-- person can not be held to have-- (a) breached any code of professional etiquette or ethics; or (b) departed from
-- accepted standards of professional conduct." "Applies if": no when unmet, worded as this section's protection only.
GIVEN `I acted honestly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `given under the Act about a human rights complaint` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Protected`
`s 99 -- protected` `I acted honestly` `given under the Act about a human rights complaint` MEANS
    IF `I acted honestly` AND `given under the Act about a human rights complaint`
    THEN `yes: you are not liable civilly, criminally or under an administrative process for giving it, and are not taken to have breached professional ethics or standards (s 99(2), (3))`
    ELSE `no: s 99 gives no protection on these facts; it applies to information given honestly under the Act to the commissioner or another entity about a human rights complaint (s 99(1))`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 100 -- an anonymity direction (a prohibition on me, if one is given)`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 100 "(1) If ... the commissioner considers that the preservation of anonymity of a person who is, or has been,
-- involved in the complaint is necessary to protect the work security, privacy or any human right of the person, the
-- commissioner may give a direction prohibiting the disclosure of information that identifies, or is likely to lead to
-- the identification of, the person. (2) A person must comply with a direction unless the person has a reasonable
-- excuse. Maximum penalty-- (a) in the case of an individual--35 penalty units; or (b) in the case of a corporation--
-- 170 penalty units." The value of a penalty unit is set under the Penalties and Sentences Act 1992 (not deposited):
-- the answer is in penalty units.
--
-- The regulative rule: while a direction applies to me and I have no reasonable excuse, I SHANT disclose. The period is
-- the one in question (the trace waits it out); disclosing in it is the breach.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act done`
`s 100(2) -- my duty not to disclose` MEANS
    PARTY `I`
    SHANT `disclose information that identifies the protected person`
    WITHIN 1
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `I` BECAUSE "disclosure contrary to an anonymity direction without reasonable excuse (s 100(2)): an offence, maximum 35 penalty units for an individual"

DECLARE `Anonymity` IS ONE OF
    `no breach: no anonymity direction covers the information`
    `no breach: you have a reasonable excuse (s 100(2))`
    `no breach: you have complied with the direction by not disclosing the information (s 100(2))`
    `breach: disclosing the information contrary to the direction is an offence, maximum 35 penalty units for an individual (s 100(2)(a))`

GIVEN `a direction covers the information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I disclosed it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Anonymity`
`s 100 -- anonymity` `a direction covers the information` `I have a reasonable excuse` `I disclosed it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a direction covers the information`
        THEN `no breach: no anonymity direction covers the information`
        IF `I have a reasonable excuse`
        THEN `no breach: you have a reasonable excuse (s 100(2))`
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER EVALTRACE `s 100(2) -- my duty not to disclose` 0
                               (IF `I disclosed it`
                                THEN LIST (EVENT `I` `disclose information that identifies the protected person` 0), (WAITUNTIL 2)
                                ELSE LIST (WAITUNTIL 2))
            WHEN FULFILLED THEN `no breach: you have complied with the direction by not disclosing the information (s 100(2))`
            OTHERWISE `breach: disclosing the information contrary to the direction is an offence, maximum 35 penalty units for an individual (s 100(2)(a))`
